<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constitution Act, 1982</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1982">1982</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Constitution Act, 1982 is part of the Constitution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, enacted together with the Canada Act 1982 of the British Parliament. It patriated the constitution, ending the need for British approval of amendments, set out a domestic amending formula and entrenched the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms. The government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> did not approve it, a source of continuing constitutional debate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constitution-act-1982.jpg" alt="Constitution Act, 1982" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Coat_of_arms_of_Canada.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
